<h4>C. The &laquo;custody of the eyes&raquo; challenge</h4>
<p>The desert fathers practiced &laquo;custody of the eyes&raquo; &mdash; the discipline of controlling what they looked at. For one day this week, practice it deliberately: when you see someone attractive, instead of a second look, say a quick prayer for them (&laquo;Lord, bless this person, your beloved child&raquo;). When an impure image appears on your screen, close it immediately. When curiosity pulls you toward gossip about someone's relationships or body, change the subject or stay silent. At the end of the day, write down what you noticed:</p>
